/F1 5.061870086203133 Tf
(LAYOUT CONSTRAINTS  \(a netlist cannot carry these\)) Tj
() Tj
T* () Tj
T* (1.  FRONT face carries U1 and nothing else.  The lens holder) Tj
() Tj
T* (     seats against it and must sit flat.  Everything else) Tj
() Tj
T* (     goes on the BACK, decoupling caps included.) Tj
() Tj
T* () Tj
T* (2.  Mounting holes centre on the OPTICAL centre, not the) Tj
() Tj
T* (     package centre.  Offset \(X,Y\) = \(-1.271, -0.148\) mm) Tj
() Tj
T* (     per onsemi case outline 570CK note 12.  The package) Tj
() Tj
T* (     will look off-centre between the screws - that is) Tj
() Tj
T* (     correct.  2 x M2 at 20 mm spacing, ~30 mm sq board.) Tj
() Tj
T* () Tj
T* (3.  Route the ten MIPI traces FIRST.  100 ohm differential,) Tj
() Tj
T* (     over unbroken ground on layer 2.  Match each pair to) Tj
() Tj
T* (     within 0.1 mm.  Keep short, avoid vias.) Tj
() Tj
T* (     Pair polarity is NOT consistent:) Tj
() Tj
T* (        DATA0  C9 = P,  C10 = N) Tj
() Tj
T* (        DATA1  C11 = N, C12 = P     <-- reversed) Tj
() Tj
T* (        DATA2  E9 = P,  E10 = N) Tj
() Tj
T* (        DATA3  E11 = P, E12 = N) Tj
() Tj
T* (        CLK    D11 = P, D12 = N) Tj
() Tj
T* () Tj
T* (4.  Stackup:  L1 front = sensor + MIPI.   L2 = solid ground,) Tj
() Tj
T* (     route NOTHING through it.   L3 = the three rails as) Tj
() Tj
T* (     patches.   L4 back = everything else.) Tj
() Tj
T* () Tj
T* (5.  Place C1-C11 / C25-C27 hard against their ball clusters.) Tj
() Tj
T* (     Distance matters more than value.) Tj
() Tj
T* () Tj
T* (6.  Keep the U4 - L1 - C23 switching loop tight.) Tj
() Tj
T* (     Route FB_1V2 as a signal trace, away from SW_1V2.) Tj
() Tj
T* () Tj
T* (7.  U5 goes beside the sensor F6/E6 balls, not beside J1.) Tj
() Tj
T* () Tj
T* (8.  NT1 is the ONLY join between AGND and GND.  Place it) Tj
() Tj
T* (     deliberately, near the sensor.) Tj
() Tj
T* () Tj
T* (9.  Add a test pad on each of +2V8, +1V8, +1V2 so every) Tj
() Tj
T* (     rail can be metered before the board meets a Pi.) Tj
() Tj
T* () Tj
T* (10. Cable must be REVERSE type \(opposite-face contacts\).) Tj
() Tj
T* (     Meter +3V3 continuity end to end before first power-up.) Tj
() Tj
T* (     Never substitute a display cable.) Tj
